{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>But You, O my doe</b> — Let it not arise in your heart how David calls [Him thus], for HaShem is his doe and his light and his salvation and his help, and all of these are in construct state (מקדים), for his intent is to declare the power of the Most High that he received."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:14.295082479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}